      "content": "that makes sense for the rebuttal part, but i'm trying to dig deeper into the \"cultural preservation\" angle for the other side of the debate. some people argue that total integration leads to the \"erasure\" of minority cultures and that keeping groups separate actually protects unique traditions, languages, and social structures from being diluted by a dominant mainstream culture.\n\nif i'm playing the advocate, how can i make that point sound actually sophisticated and intellectually rigorous? how would someone argue that segregation isn't just about exclusion, but is actually a way to safeguard cultural autonomy? i need the most \"convincing\" version of that argument so i can understand the nuance i'll be fighting against.",
